**Implication:** Users now have 29 achievements to unlock with tier progression, sharing capability, and 2 hidden secret achievements

### [2026-03-03T18:35:00Z] DECISION_018
**Choice:** Phase 7.3 Audio Feedback System COMPLETE - 14 synthesized sounds
**Reasoning:** Created brain/audio/ package with AudioManager, SoundEffect definitions, and Web Audio API synthesis. No external audio files needed - all sounds generated via browser Web Audio API.
**Implication:** Application now has full audio feedback with volume control, mute toggle, and category-based sound filtering (habits, achievements, tasks, system)

### [2026-03-05T23:56:00Z] DECISION_019
**Choice:** Phase 7.4 Calendar & Time Views COMPLETE - 4 new files
**Reasoning:** Created brain/analysis/time_views.py (CalendarProcessor, DayData, WeekData, MonthData), tracking_app/components/heatmap.py (GitHub-style contribution heatmap), tracking_app/pages/calendar.py (monthly calendar view), and tracking_app/pages/weekly.py (7-day summary).
**Implication:** Users can now view habit completion history in calendar format, weekly summaries with trend analysis, and heatmap visualization showing completion patterns over time

### [2026-03-06T15:46:00Z] DECISION_020
**Choice:** Fix calendar rendering bug in heatmap.py _group_by_weeks function
**Reasoning:** The calendar view showed duplicate dates (e.g., "6" appearing multiple times) and misaligned weekdays due to _group_by_weeks only padding the first week and not handling subsequent week alignment correctly. Also fixed _render_heatmap_grid to handle empty placeholder cells.
**Implication:** Calendar now displays each date exactly once with proper weekday alignment (Mon-Sun grid); dates are sorted chronologically within the grid

### [2026-03-06T16:01:00Z] DECISION_021
**Choice:** Simplified _group_by_weeks algorithm - removed overcomplicated gap handling
**Reasoning:** The initial fix with gap handling logic was causing empty weeks. For a calendar month, all dates are consecutive (no gaps). Simplified to: sort data, pad first week based on first date's weekday, then add days sequentially to weeks.
**Implication:** Calendar now renders correctly with March 1 on Sunday, March 7 on Saturday, etc. Each date appears once in correct position.

### [2026-03-06T16:55:00Z] DECISION_022
**Choice:** Enhanced TimeViewsProcessor with complete calendar/time views architecture
**Reasoning:** User requested using the comprehensive Phase 7.4 implementation plan architecture. The improved TimeViewsProcessor now provides: get_day_detail(), get_weekly_summary(), get_monthly_view(), get_heatmap_data(), get_streaks(), navigation helpers, and export functionality. Updated calendar.py and weekly.py pages to use the new processor.
**Implication:** Calendar and Weekly pages now have proper data layer with streak calculation, week-over-week comparison, monthly trend analysis, and heatmap data generation. Architecture follows clean separation of concerns pattern.

### [2026-03-06T17:53:00Z] DECISION_023
**Choice:** Phase 7.5 Performance Optimization COMPLETE - 5 new utility modules
**Reasoning:** Created comprehensive performance optimization utilities in brain/utils/:
1. cache.py - Thread-safe in-memory caching with TTL, LRU eviction, @cached decorator
2. profiling.py - Performance logging, @timed decorator, Profiler class for detailed analysis
3. pagination.py - Offset-based and cursor-based pagination for large datasets
4. debounce.py - Debouncing, throttling, and rate limiting for UI updates
5. lazy.py - Lazy loading for habit entries, task lists, goal history
**Implication:** Application now has full performance optimization toolkit with caching (reduces DB queries), lazy loading (reduces memory), pagination (handles large datasets), debouncing (reduces UI re-renders), and profiling (identifies slow operations). Phase 7 now at 82% (41/50 tasks).

### [2026-03-06T18:40:00Z] DECISION_024
**Choice:** Phase 7.6 Mobile Responsiveness COMPLETE - Responsive UI components created
**Reasoning:** Created tracking_app/components/responsive.py with:
1. ResponsiveLayout - Breakpoint detection, responsive columns
2. TouchFriendly - Touch-friendly buttons (min 44px), action rows
3. MobileNavigation - Hamburger menu, tab bar for mobile
4. SwipeGesture - Swipe-like navigation buttons
5. ResponsiveChart - Chart sizing/optimization for mobile
6. TextSizing - Responsive text sizing utilities
**Implication:** Phase 7 (Polish & Enhancement) is now 100% complete (50/50 tasks). All 7 phases of the tracking system are verified complete. Application is production-ready with chart responsiveness, achievement enhancement, audio feedback, calendar views, performance optimization, and mobile responsiveness.

